# Deny everything, then re-admit only what `vite build` and `go build` read.
# `*` matches dotfiles, so this is also what keeps .git out of the context --
# which is the point: with no .git, getGitInfo() in web/vite.config.ts cannot
# fall back to `git rev-parse`, so the version stamp comes from the build args
# or is honestly wrong rather than quietly stale.
*

!package.json
!pnpm-lock.yaml
!pnpm-workspace.yaml
!shared
!sdk
!scripts
!web
!docker

# ...minus the parts of those that are not build inputs. A re-admitted directory
# re-admits its whole subtree, so these have to be named explicitly.
sdk/node_modules
web/node_modules
web/dist
web/e2e
web/playwright.config.ts
web/playwright-report
web/test-results
web/README.md
docker/serve/mica-serve
